{"page_id": "rotation_skew-rsb3ec4b87_rot90-p1", "markdown": "# KENNETH WOODS\n\nPORTFOLIO MANAGEMENT PROGRAM\n\nStrategic direction\n\nGS derives its revenues through a public / private market focused business model which for the most part capitalizes on fees and commissions for services and structured products. As the environment for global investment banks deters, management at GS is focused on targeting the market share of peers who scale back in many markets across the globe. Credit Suisse and Deutsche Bank in particular have begun scaling back their US and European operations in an effort to refocus their businesses and GS is a prime hunter for their share of the market. The Company has publicly stated that in the US market they will look to strengthen their share of the Institutional Client Services market.\n\nBeyond this, the Company has deployed (and is continuing to deploy) a franchise mix strategy that minimizes their exposure to the riskiness of trading revenues in FICC, focusing more on investment banking and investment management (Exhibit 3). The Company's investment banking revenues now\n\nExhibit 3\n\nHistorical revenue mix-\n\n13%\n\n19%\n\n- Underwriting\n- FICC\n\n- Financial advisory\n- Investing and lending\n\n15%\n\n17%\n\n16%\n\n21%\n\n7%\n\n31%\n\n35%\n\n- Equities\n- Investment management\n\n17%\n\n20%\n\n25%\n\n18%\n\n16%\n\n22%\n\n21%\n\n5%\n\n7%\n\nFY 2010A\n\n29%\n\n7%\n\nFY 2011A\n\n29%\n\n25%\n\n24%\n\n21%\n\n6%\n\n6%\n\n12%\n\nFY 2012A\n\nFY 2013A\n\n20%\n\n23%\n\n7%\n\n12%\n\nFY 2014A\n\n10%\n\n11%\n\nFY 2015A\n\nOn a geographic level, GS revenues are derived primarily from North America, however on a profit level, the Company has strong earnings power in the\n\n\"EMEA\" and \"Asia and Oceania\" segments. This is a strong positive for the Company's positioning as their most operationally effective markets also provide the greatest future growth avenues (Exhibit 4).\n\n10", "width": 2200, "height": 1700, "blocks": [{"kind": "heading", "text": "KENNETH WOODS", "bbox": {"x": 2146.8598913795613, "y": 74.37499805208328, "width": 31.884081620908876, "height": 272.7083333333335}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PORTFOLIO MANAGEMENT PROGRAM", "bbox": {"x": 2125.6038527765018, "y": 70.83332983593762, "width": 17.713389189346817, "height": 279.79166666666663}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Strategic direction", "bbox": {"x": 1973.2689074289535, "y": 527.7083309806549, "width": 42.51210432313681, "height": 329.37499999999994}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "GS derives its revenues through a public / private market focused business model which for the most part capitalizes on fees and commissions for services and structured products. As the environment for global investment banks deters, management at GS is focused on targeting the market share of peers who scale back in many markets across the globe. Credit Suisse and Deutsche Bank in particular have begun scaling back their US and European operations in an effort to refocus their businesses and GS is a prime hunter for their share of the market. The Company has publicly stated that in the US market they will look to strengthen their share of the Institutional Client Services market.", "bbox": {"x": 1522.1096326058885, "y": 527.4777185748918, "width": 370.4506497836152, "height": 1105.4163360595703}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Beyond this, the Company has deployed (and is continuing to deploy) a franchise mix strategy that minimizes their exposure to the riskiness of trading revenues in FICC, focusing more on investment banking and investment management (Exhibit 3). The Company's investment banking revenues now", "bbox": {"x": 1317.874353762026, "y": 527.7083232933409, "width": 155.87770458964735, "height": 1051.875}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Exhibit 3", "bbox": {"x": 1165.5394455617277, "y": 527.7083320642361, "width": 35.426744593130465, "height": 152.29166666666669}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Historical revenue mix-", "bbox": {"x": 1087.600630456329, "y": 548.9